  "notes": [
    "Stats follow the army list's table (pp. 168-169). The Westphalia chapter (pp. 86-88) gives some differently: Cuirassier Hand-to-Hand 8, Morale 4, Reliable; Garde du Corps Hand-to-Hand 3, Morale 4, Heavy Cavalry D1; Guard Chevauleger without Marauder; Line infantry with Mixed Formation rather than Poor Mixed Formation. Agree with your opponent which to use.",
    "The Confederation of the Rhine list's maximums and minimums are per every 1,000 points unless otherwise stated (p. 172). The builder applies them as written, which is right for armies up to 1,000 points; scale them up yourself for larger armies.",
    "A Divisional commander must take brigades of his own nationality; the Rheinbund brigade is the exception."
  ],
  "specialRules": [
    "Westphalian infantry follows the French infantry special rules, but does not have Pas de Charge.",
    "Lacking Initiative (Line and Light infantry): a unit lacking initiative can't make initiative moves except to change formation or facing; any other move must be by orders.",
    "Line infantry: Lie Down, Must Form Square, Column of Companies, Close Column and Poor Mixed Formation. Light infantry and the Guard Jäger also have Light Infantry Mixed Formation; the Jäger-Karabiniers have Rifle Mixed Formation and Light Infantry Mixed Formation.",
    "Westphalian cavalry can use Deep Formation and Cavalry Mixed Formation.",
    "Guard Chevauleger: two of the six dice it rolls in hand-to-hand can count as lance attacks.",
    "The Guard Grenadiers' regimental guns use the regimental artillery profile, with smoothbore foot artillery in place of battalion artillery."
  ],
  "alliesRules": [
    {
      "maxPercent": 25,
      "note": "any one allied list (Confederation of the Rhine)"
    }
  ]
}
